1
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:19,330
Champagne flutes on the limestone ledge

2
00:00:19,450 --> 00:00:23,140
Three dozen stories above the avenue hedge

3
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:26,450
You’re leaning back in your linen shirt

4
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:31,000
Laughing too loud so the truth won't hurt

5
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:34,840
The sun drops low like a minted coin

6
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:38,710
Where the rusted girders and brick adjoin

7
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,450
Everyone’s acting like August stayed

8
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:46,310
While the terrace shadows begin to trade

9
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:50,300
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

10
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,130
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

11
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:57,840
You look at the skyline, not at me

12
00:00:57,900 --> 00:01:01,880
Like a ship already out to sea

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,900
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,900
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,820
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

16
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,710
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

17
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:21,700
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

18
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,700
In the brightest hour of a dying year

19
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:33,360
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

20
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,920
Your best friend’s spinning an old French record

21
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:41,730
Our history’s suddenly strangely checkered

22
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:45,620
You hand me your jacket, the lining’s torn

23
00:01:45,700 --> 00:01:49,350
Swearing this fever is newly born

24
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:53,220
But I know the cadence of an exit line

25
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:57,030
Dressed up in vintage cabernet wine

26
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:00,550
You kiss my collarbone, quick and polite

27
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:04,760
Beneath the amber Edison string-bulb light

28
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:08,800
There’s a sudden bite in the evening air

29
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:12,630
And you trace the rim of your crystal ware

30
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:16,340
You look at the skyline, not at me

31
00:02:16,400 --> 00:02:20,380
Like a ship already out to sea

32
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:24,310
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust

33
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:28,300
All of our promises ground into velvet dust

34
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:32,300
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

35
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:36,300
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail

36
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:40,300
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

37
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:44,300
In the brightest hour of a dying year

38
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:51,780
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight

39
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,550
Remember July on the fire escape?

40
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,450
When every tomorrow had a reckless shape!

41
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,250
Now you’re folding your secrets into your cuff

42
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,050
As if wanting you once wasn't quite enough!

43
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,450
Don't tell me the season is just a phase

44
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:07,680
When I see the frost in your sideways gaze!

45
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,900
It’s copper on the terrace, gold turning to rust!

46
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,900
All of our promises ground into velvet dust!

47
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,730
Dance me to the edge of the balcony rail

48
00:03:19,800 --> 00:03:23,620
Before the warm trade winds begin to fail!

49
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:27,600
You’re holding my waist like a souvenir

50
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:31,510
In the brightest hour of a dying year

51
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:40,090
Yeah, it’s copper on the terrace tonight!

52
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,820
Copper and rust on the avenue

53
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:48,720
The air turns sharp between me and you

54
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:52,440
Just a souvenir

55
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:56,900
in the fading glow
